name: sim.pushUserEvent
description: Pushes a user-triggered event. Messages are received asynchronously via the sysCall_event callback function and via the plugin sim_message_eventcallback_events message call
luaSynopsis: sim.pushUserEvent(string event, int handle int uid, dict eventData, int options = 0)
pythonSynopsis: sim.pushUserEvent(string event, int handle int uid, table eventData, int options = 0)
inputs:
1. event: event name
2. handle: optional handle associated with the event. Can be -1
3. uid: optional unique id associated with the event. Can be -1
4. eventData: event data
5. options: bit-coded:
    - bit0 set (1): event can be merged with a previous, same event
outputs:
replacedBy:
- name: pushEvent, class: app, file: app_pushEvent.method
